# Model UUID and Slug Convention

## UUID Primary Key

Every Django model in this project uses a UUID primary key via `UUIDModel`:

```python
from apps.common.models import UUIDModel, SlugMixin

class MyModel(UUIDModel, SlugMixin):
    ...
```

`UUIDModel` provides: `id = UUIDField(primary_key=True, default=uuid.uuid4, editable=False)`

**The only exception is `users.User`** which already has a UUID PK baked into `AbstractBaseUser`.

## Auto-generated Slug

Every new Django model also inherits `SlugMixin` which adds:
- `slug = SlugField(max_length=255, unique=True, db_index=True, blank=True)`
- Auto-filled on first save from `get_slug_source()` via `assign_unique_slug()`
- Stable once set — never rewritten when the source field changes
- Readonly in all admin forms

Override `get_slug_source()` to control which field the slug derives from:

```python
def get_slug_source(self) -> str:
    return self.name  # or self.title, self.full_name, etc.
```

**Exceptions (slug only):**
- `users.User` — login model, excluded by design
- Any other model only if explicitly stated in the task

## Rules for AI

- Do NOT ask for slug values in admin forms or API create payloads — generate them
- Do NOT make slug fields editable in API serializers
- Make slug readonly in Django Admin (`readonly_fields`)
- Use `apps.common.slugs.assign_unique_slug()` — do not write custom slug logic inline
